the templates are:
    *a person* supports *a team*.
    *a person* is a royal supporter of *a player*.

the knowledge base citizenship_including includes these resources:
    examples/moreExamples/testing/citizenship_premier,
    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mcalejo/LogicalEnglish2/main/examples/moreExamples/royal_family.

the knowledge base citizenship_including includes:
    queen victoria supports man city.
    edward supports arsenal.
    george supports liverpool.

    a person is a royal supporter of a player if
        the person is an ancestor of elizabeth and
        the person supports a team and
        the player plays for the team.

scenario one is:
    % We need to include the facts from royal_family's scenario to make the ancestor rules work,
    % because scenarios are not included from resources.
    queen victoria is a parent of edward.
    edward is a parent of george.
    george is a parent of george vi.
    george vi is a parent of elizabeth.

    one expects answers [
        "queen victoria is a royal supporter of erling haaland",
        "queen victoria is a royal supporter of kevin de bruyne",
        "edward is a royal supporter of bukayo saka",
        "edward is a royal supporter of martin odegaard",
        "george is a royal supporter of mohamed salah",
        "george is a royal supporter of virgil van dijk"
    ].

query one is:
    which person is a royal supporter of which player.
